USER_EMAIL	VARCHAR2(150)	Email address of the user
USER_TYPE	VARCHAR2(20)	Internal or External user (INTERNAL, EXTERNAL)
PROJECT_NAME	VARCHAR2(100)	(Optional) Project the user is part of
TEAM_NAME	VARCHAR2(100)	Team or department name
USER_TEAM_DL	VARCHAR2(150)	Team distribution list or group email
SERVICE_POC_NAME	VARCHAR2(100)	Name of the person responsible for the service
SERVICE_POC_EMAIL	VARCHAR2(150)	Email of the POC
ENVIRONMENT	VARCHAR2(50)	Environment (e.g., DEV, QA, PROD)
REGION	VARCHAR2(50)	(Optional) Region like US-EAST, EU-WEST, etc.
IS_ACTIVE	CHAR(1)	Whether the mapping is active (Y/N)
CREATED_AT	DATE	Record creation timestamp
UPDATED_AT	DATE	Last updated timestamp
COMMENTS	VARCHAR2(500)	(Optional) Notes or additional info

Column Naming Notes
	•	Followed Oracle-style conventions (uppercase, underscore-separated).
	•	Descriptive names for clarity (e.g., SERVICE_POC_EMAIL instead of just POC_EMAIL).
	•	Consider constraints like NOT NULL on SERVICE_ID, USER_NAME, etc.
	•	Add indexes on frequently queried columns like SERVICE_ID, USER_EMAIL.

Optional Enhancements
	•	Create a separate SERVICE_DETAILS table to normalize service info if many users share a service.
	•	Same for TEAM_DETAILS and USER_DETAILS if you’re storing more metadata.

